Filter commands:

grep ---> global regular expression print / pattern.
	 ex:  grep "LINUX" new.txt (it only gives matched sentance)

	-n ---> to get line numbers.
	-i ---> ignore the case.
	-v --->invert the match.
	-w --> exact match
	-l --> display the file name.,
	-h ---> only display the search line without filename.
	-o ---> only disply the searched word.
	-c ---> to disply the no of times the pattern is present.
	-$ ---> search at the end of the text input.
				ex: grep "linux$" new.txt
			
	-^ ---> search at the begining of t6he text input.\
				ex:	grep "^unix" new.txt
	

 grep "linux" new.txt  1.txt
