data manupulations:

SED: --> sed command in linux stands for stream editor and it can perform lots of functions like searching, find and replace, insertion or deletion.
synax:
	sed options [SCRIPT] []Filename]
	
SEARCH AND REPLACE

	ex:
		 sed 's/linux/unix/g' new.txt -----> it wii do replace all occurence of linux with unix.
	
	 sed '1s/linux/unix/g' new.txt  --> to change first occurence of linux replace with unix.



--- replace second and more occurence of word linux with unix.
 		sed '2,$s/linux/unix/g' new.txt
	
--->replace only 2nd of the word linux with unix in second line to 4th line.

		 sed '2,4 s/linux/unix/g' new.txt

DELETE LINES:

--> To delete 2nd line 
 	sed '2d' new.txt

---> To delete 2nd and 3rd line
	sed '2,3 d' new.txt

---> To delete last line
	 sed '$ d' new.txt
 sed '$ d' new.txt

---> To delete all lines starting with tab
 	sed '/^\t/d' new.txt

---> To delete the lines ends with (.)
		sed '/\.$/d' new.txt
-----------------------------
ADDING A LINE BEFORE AND AFTER A SEARCHED PATTERN
---
--> add a line after word linux occurs
	sed '/linux/a "This is the new line after word linux" ' new.txt
--> add a line before word linux occurs
	 sed '/linux/i "This is the new line before word linux" ' m.txt
	
-------
PRINTING LINES

--> To display 2nd to 4th line
	 sed -n '2,4 p' new.txt
---> Start  from line 2 and print every second line.
	sed -n '2~2 p' new.txt
---> to print from line 2 every 2nd line in between the range.
	sed -n '1,6 {2~2p}' new.txt


---------
MERGING 2 OR MORE LINES	

---> start from 4th line and merge 2 lines 
	
	 sed '4N; s/\n/ /g' new.txt
----> to merge more than 2 lines
 sed '2{N; N; N; s/\n/ /g;}' new.txt
---->
sed '2N; 3N; 4N; s/\n/ /g' new.txt



Important notations in sed command:

	-N ---> add next line to pattern space immediatly.
	-g ---> global
	- -i --> (option): in file editing
	-p ---> display the contents
	-d ---> delete the pattern space
	-a ---> inserting a line after the searched pattern
	 i ---> inserting a line before the searched pattern.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

AWK COMMAND:

	It is used for database manipulation command. It enables a programmer to write tiny effective in the form of statements.


to print all the content of the file
	 ls -l | awk '{print $0}'
to print only last index of the file
 ls -l | awk '{print $NF}'

Imaportant notations:

	-$0  	: indicate complete line
	-$1  	: indicate 1st word in the line
	-$NF 	: indicates last word/column in a line
	-$NF-1	: incicates second last word / column in a line


example:
EMP_ID Name Domain Location Salary
101 Ram PD hyd 50000
102 Ravi STA bangalore 75000
103 Kumar DV HYD 70000
104 Teja DFT bangalore 60000
105 Anil STA HYD 50000
106 mani PNR bangalore 60000

--> to get id and name 
 awk '{print $1,$2}' awk.txt

---> to get all sta engineer name, location and salary
 awk '$3 == "STA" {print $2,$4,$5}' awk.txt


